Domain: com.anthropic.claudefordesktop
Format: .mobileconfig (managed preference)

<dict>
  <key>inferenceProvider</key>
  <string>gateway</string>
  <key>inferenceGatewayBaseUrl</key>
  <string>{gateway}</string>
  <key>inferenceGatewayApiKey</key>
  <string>&lt;loopback-secret-from-~/Library/Application Support/systemprompt/bridge-loopback.key&gt;</string>
  <key>inferenceGatewayAuthScheme</key>
  <string>bearer</string>
  <key>disableEssentialTelemetry</key>
  <string>true</string>
  <key>disableNonessentialTelemetry</key>
  <string>true</string>
  <key>disableNonessentialServices</key>
  <string>false</string>
  <key>disableAutoUpdates</key>
  <string>true</string>
  <key>disableDeploymentModeChooser</key>
  <string>true</string>
  <!-- Optional. Omit for unrestricted egress (the default). Loopback-only is
       the air-gapped/regulated posture; apply it with
       `install --apply --egress-allowed-hosts loopback` so the Bridge keeps
       this payload in step.
  <key>coworkEgressAllowedHosts</key>
  <array>
    <string>127.0.0.1</string>
  </array>
  -->
</dict>

The bridge's own manifest signing key is a second managed domain, not a key in
Claude's (Claude Desktop ignores keys it does not know and logs a warning):
Domain: io.systemprompt.{config_dir}
<dict>
  <key>manifestPubkey</key>
  <string>&lt;base64 ed25519 pubkey&gt;</string>
</dict>
